title: Graduation
---
<<declare $playerName = "Holder">>
<<gathervars>>
After everything this year, you did it. You scraped your grade
together enough to graduate!

As others threw their hats in the air, you held onto yours,
preferring something solid. A reminder that even when things
were rough, you still made it.

<<jump FullEnd>>
===

title: GraduationWithFaust
---
After everything this year, you did it. You scraped your grade
together enough to graduate!

As others threw their hats in the air, you held onto yours,
preferring something solid. A reminder that even when things
were rough, you still made it.
<<moodSwitch>>
<<jump GoodFaust>>
===

title: GoodNiko
---
Birds tweet softly as a summer breeze moves the trees outside.
Swallows loop across the blue sky beyond the locked window.

Niko: "Are you admiring the birds, my dove?" He approaches
quietly.

Niko: "You look breathtaking,"

You are dressed carefully, styled exactly how he likes. To him,
you are delicate. Precious.

His dove. His dove in a gilded cage.

Niko: "Don't you like it?" He gestures to the table.

Croissants, pain au chocolat, and pastries cover it.

Niko: "I wanted you to feel like you were in Paris, dining
beside La Seine."

Niko: "Because, ma chérie, you deserve the best,"

He lifts your hand, kissing each knuckle slowly. A quiet
reminder of who you belong to.

He listens to distant church bells.

Niko: "Isn't today your graduation?" He tilts his head.

You: "It was. I forgot about it,"

He smiles brightly.

Niko: "An éclair?" He offers it gently.

You: "Could we go for a walk today?" You miss the outside air.

He sets the éclair down, displeased.

Niko: "I can open the window. It might feel like a walk by a
river."

Niko: "You know why you can't go out,"

He stands, kissing your forehead.

Niko: "It's alright. We all make mistakes,"

He cracks the window open slightly, the key resting around his
neck.

Niko: "It's a beautiful day,"

You smile. You agree. It is a beautiful day.

And maybe this isn't so bad.
<<jump FullEnd>>
===

title: GoodFaust
---
You stop by the cafe for one last campus coffee when Faust
approaches you.

Faust: "Those answers I gave you? Most of them were lies."

You stare at him as he looks away, shifting.

Faust: "I cared too much about how I looked. Even answering
your questions felt...wrong."

He hesitates.

Faust: "I didn't want to seem weak. So I lied."

Silence lingers between you.
<<jump FullEnd>>
===

title: SalemRift
---
A terrible feeling grips you, the need to find Salem becoming
unbearable. You decide to go to her dorm.

Something flickers at the edge of your vision, glitching. You
turn quickly. Nothing.

Your heart pounds. You feel watched.

A voice whispers.

"Find me,"

Your mind dulls, your body moving on its own. The panic fades
as you follow.

At the rift, everything is wrong. A dark space stretches
endlessly, a rocky hill leading toward a dim blue light.

Whispers fill your ears, unknowable, your mind rejecting them.

You walk forward anyway.

You: "Why am I walking?"

The thought feels distant. Not yours.

You climb the hill, stone shifting beneath your feet.

Then you see it. A massive archway glowing blue, dust swirling
around it like light.

It feels wrong. Too big. Too alive.

The whispers urge you closer.

Then—

You see her.

Salem.

Your trance breaks. You gasp and run toward her.

She turns.

Salem: "{$playerName}, you came!"

Her voice echoes. Her pupils are blown wide as she sways,
smiling too wide.

Something is wrong.

Salem: "I'm so happy...you came. You cared...you spoke up for
me,"

She drifts closer.

You: "Salem...what are you doing?"

Salem: "I'm going to a new dream. All my sadness will disappear,"

Her eyes snap open.

Salem: "A fresh start...a better world,"

She laughs, unstable, grabbing your arms tightly.

Salem: "I'm so tired of this dream. So much pain...I want
something happy,"

She looks at you.

Salem: "You're happy for me, right?"

You frown.

You: "Don't do it,"

She freezes.

Salem: "What?"

You: "You'll lose everything. Your friends, your family...me."

You: "Without pain, you lose everything else too."

Silence.

Then she cries.

Salem: "I'm just so tired. Why is everything so cruel?"

She sobs. You pull her into a hug.

You: "I know,"

You hold her as she cries.

You: "Let's leave together,"

She looks up and nods.

You guide her away. Behind you, the gate goes silent.
<<jump FullEnd>>
===

title: FullEnd
